question:
A circle is given by x² + (y – 1)² = 1. Another circle C touches it externally and also the x-axis, then the locus of its centre is
(A) {(x, y) : x² = 4y} ∪ {(x, y) : y ≤ 0}
(B) {(x, y) : x² + (y – 1)² = 4} ∪ {(x, y) : y ≤ 0}
(C) {(x, y) : x² = y} ∪ {(0, y) : y ≤ 0}
(D) {(x, y) : x² = 4y} ∪ {(0, y) : y ≤ 0}
